sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ga02-27> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "The bregma is the last bone to form and is still soft after birth" ;
    dct:description "The bregma (the top of the skull) is the last bone to be formed and is still soft in children after birth, more so in man than in other animals because man's brain is the most fluid and largest." ;
    delphi:context "Aristotle, On the Generation of Animals (De Generatione Animalium), Book II; translated by Arthur Platt, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: Humans, compared with other animals with a brain" ;
    dct:type "empirical-generalization" .
}

